>
  <p>
    <strong>englishtoburmese.com</strong> is a specialized, free online translator built for anyone who needs to bridge English and Burmese (Myanmar) accurately and quickly. Whether you are a student learning language nuances, a traveler preparing for a journey to Yangon or Bagan, a family member keeping in touch across continents, or a professional reviewing documents, our goal is to make translation frictionless.
  </p>

  <h2>What you can translate</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Typed or pasted English text:</strong> Full support for English phrases, emails, and <a href="/#usage">everyday sentences</a> up to 20,000 characters.</li>
    <li><strong>Spoken English (Talk):</strong> Dictate English directly using your browser's microphone to auto-populate the input box.</li>
    <li><strong>Burmese speech output:</strong> Listen to natural Burmese pronunciation of your translation results with our audio playback engine.</li>
    <li><strong>Full documents:</strong> Instant text extraction and side-by-side translation for <a href="/#file">TXT, Word (.docx), and PDF files</a> up to 12 MB.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Why a dedicated English to Burmese tool?</h2>
  <p>
    Many popular multi-language portals treat Burmese as an afterthought, often resulting in font encoding mix-ups between the obsolete Zawgyi encoding and standard Unicode. Our platform is exclusively tuned for <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burmese_language" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Burmese (မြန်မာဘာသာ)</a>, guaranteeing output that adheres strictly to the official <a href="https://unicode.org/standard/standard.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Unicode Standard</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <p>
    When you input text, it is processed through neural machine translation models optimized for English-to-Burmese linguistic syntax, accurately translating English Subject-Verb-Object (SVO) structures into natural Burmese Subject-Object-Verb (SOV) order. The rendered Myanmar text is formatted with proper tone markers and virama ligatures that paste seamlessly into Facebook, Viber, Telegram, Gmail, and word processors.
  </p>

  <h2>Our philosophy: Open &amp; accessible</h2>
  <p>
    We believe foundational language tools should be immediately available to everyone without barriers. You do not need to create an account, download third-party software, or provide personal information to translate text, upload documents, or listen to audio.
  </p>
  <p>
    Machine translation provides an excellent working draft, but for critical immigration, medical, academic, or court proceedings, we recommend verification by a certified human translator. Please consult our <a href="/disclaimer">Disclaimer</a> and <a href="/terms">Terms and Conditions</a> for usage policies.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions, feedback &amp; suggestions</h2>
  <p>
    Have questions, found an error, or have suggestions for new features? We would love to hear from you. Visit our <a href="/contact">Contact us</a> page or explore answers in our <a href="/#faq">Frequently Asked Questions</a>.
  </p>
